# Bounce for Pharo 14

A simple bouncing ball example to get you started.

This is a markdown document, but it is, *also* wchnt source code which can be executed by clicking the Run button. The section headings and code blocks are an essential part of the syntax of the language.
 

## Schema

The **Schema** is where we write the overall shape of the data in our program. In this case we are defining three classes called `Game`, `PlayArea` and `Ball` and how they fit together.

A Game is made of or contains a PlayArea and a Ball. The PlayArea holds the dimensions of the play area. Two Ints called `width` and `height` respectively. Ball has `x` and `y` coordinates. `dx` and `dy` are the current movement in each dimension. And `rad` is radius.

Note how all three classes, their components and their relationships are defined in one place.

```
Game = PlayArea Ball
PlayArea = Int/width Int/height
Ball = Int/x Int/y Int/dx Int/dy Int/rad
```

## Construction

The **Construction** actually builds the objects with their initial data values. We use nested square bracket lists, with the class-name as the first element (with a colon in front), and the values of each field in the same order they appear in the schema. A Game is made of the PlayArea and the Ball, so it needs to be construction with constructions of those objects nested inside.

```
[:Game
  [:PlayArea 800 500]
  [:Ball 200 150 6 5 16]
]
```


## Methods

Thanks to R.I. Chalmers for the improvement to the Ball::bounced algorithm.

```
Ball::bounced = { PlayArea/r |
  newDx = if (((x + dx - rad) < 0) or ((x + dx + rad) > r.width)) { -dx } else { dx}.
  newDy = if (((y + dy - rad) < 0) or ((y + dy + rad) > r.height)) { -dy } else { dy }.
  [:Ball (x+newDx) (y+newDy) newDx newDy rad]
}

Game::step = {
  [:Game playArea ball.bounced(playArea)]
}

Ball::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  g.beginFill(0xffffff).drawCircle(x, y, rad).endFill()
}

PlayArea::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  g.beginFill(0x003300).drawRect(0, 0, width, height).endFill()
}

Game::draw = { @WCHNTGraphics/g |
  drawnPA = playArea.draw(g).
  drawnBall = ball.draw(g).
  g
}
```

## Target

```
%smalltalk

%init
| game |
game := GameAssemblage new factory.
wchntGraphics game: game.

%step
game := game step.
wchntGraphics clear.
game draw: wchntGraphics.
```
